      Let $K = bb(Q)(sqrt(-d))$ be an imaginary quadratic field of fundamental discriminant $-d < 0$. Show directly that for $d = 4$ ($K = bb(Q)(i)$) and $d = 3$ ($K = bb(Q)(sqrt(-3))$), the modular $j$-invariants are $j(i) = 1728$ and $j((1 + sqrt(-3)) \/ 2) = 0$. More generally, using the class polynomial $H_D (X) = product_([frak(a)] in op("Cl")(cal(O)_K)) (X - j(frak(a))) in bb(Z)[X]$, verify that $j(sqrt(-2)) = 8000$ and $j((1 + sqrt(-7)) \/ 2) = -3375$.
    ],
    [
      Complete the proof of Theorem 8.3 by showing explicitly that for $m = 2$, the modular polynomial is
      $ Phi_2 (X, Y) &= X^3 + Y^3 - X^2 Y^2 + 1488 (X^2 Y + X Y^2) \
        & quad - 162000 (X^2 + Y^2) + 40773375 X Y \
        & quad + 8748000000 (X + Y) - 157464000000000, $
      and factor $Phi_2 (X, X)$ over $bb(Z)$ to recover the $j$-invariants of the three orders of discriminants $-4$, $-7$, and $-8$ (namely $1728$, $-3375$, and $8000$).
    ],
    [
      Using the Main Theorem of Complex Multiplication (Theorem 8.4), determine the Galois group of the $n$-division field $K(E[n])$ over $H_K$ for an elliptic curve $E \/ H_K$ with $op("End")(E) tilde.equiv cal(O)_K$. Explain why $K(E[n]) \/ K$ is *not* always abelian (unlike $K(j(E), h(E[n])) \/ K$), and determine the exact degree $[K(E[n]) : K_((n))]$.
    ],
    [
      Use the Chowla–Selberg formula (Theorem 8.9) to compute the fundamental period $Omega$ (up to an explicit algebraic factor) for $K = bb(Q)(sqrt(-7))$ ($d = 7$, $h = 1$, $w = 2$). Compare your result with the real period of the CM elliptic curve $y^2 + x y = x^3 - x^2 - 2 x - 1$ of conductor $49$.
    ],
    [
      Prove that for any odd prime $p$, the formal group law $F_p (X, Y) = log_(F_p)^(-1)(log_(F_p)(X) + log_(F_p)(Y))$ with $log_(F_p)(T) = sum_(k >= 0) T^(p^(2 k)) \/ p^k$ satisfies
      $ F_p (X, Y) equiv X + Y - 1 / p sum_(j=1)^(p^2 - 1) binom(p^2, j) X^j Y^(p^2 - j) (mod op("deg") p^2 + 1). $
      Verify directly that every binomial coefficient $binom(p^2, j)$ for $1 <= j <= p^2 - 1$ is divisible by $p$, and check that $F_p (X, Y) equiv X + Y (mod op("deg") p^2)$.
    ],
    [
      Let $F$ be a one-dimensional formal group law over $bb(Z)_p$ of height $h >= 1$ (with $1 <= h < oo$) whose logarithm is $log_F (T) = sum_(k >= 0) T^(p^(h k)) \/ p^k$. Generalize Lemma 8.20 and Theorem 8.21 to show that for every $f in bb(Z)_p[[T]]$ and every $a >= 1$,
      $ v_p ((D^a f)(0)) >= a (1 / (p - 1) - 1 / (p^h - 1)) - O(log a). $
      Verify that for $h = 1$ the leading slope vanishes, for $h = 2$ it equals $p \/ (p^2 - 1)$, and as $h -> oo$ (approaching $hat(bb(G))_a$) it approaches $1 \/ (p - 1) = lim_(a -> oo) v_p (a!) \/ a$.
    ],
    [
      Let $E : y^2 = x^3 - x$ over $bb(Z)_p$ for an odd prime $p$. Using the Hasse invariant formula $A equiv [x^(p - 1)] (x^3 - x)^((p - 1) \/ 2) (mod p)$, show directly that $A equiv 0 (mod p)$ if and only if $p equiv 3 (mod 4)$ (i.e., $p$ is inert in $bb(Q)(i)$). For $p = 3$, compute the first $10$ terms of $log_(hat(E)) (T)$ and verify explicitly that $c_3 equiv 0 (mod 3)$ and $D^3 equiv 0 (mod 3)$.
    ],
    [
      Prove *Dwork's Lemma*: for a power series $F(X) in 1 + X bb(Q)_p[[X]]$, we have $F(X) in bb(Z)_p[[X]]$ if and only if $F(X^p) \/ F(X)^p in 1 + p X bb(Z)_p[[X]]$. Use this to give a three-line proof that the Artin–Hasse exponential $E_p (X) = exp(sum_(k >= 0) X^(p^k) \/ p^k)$ lies in $bb(Z)_p[[X]]$, and explain why the same criterion fails for $E_(p, 2)(X) = exp(sum_(k >= 0) X^(p^(2 k)) \/ p^k)$ at degree $p$.
    ],
    [
      Consider the formal group $hat(bb(G))_m (X, Y) = X + Y + X Y$ over $bb(Z)_p$ with invariant derivation $D = (1 + T) d \/ d T$. Show directly that $D^p equiv D (mod p)$ on $bb(Z)_p[[T]]$, and exhibit an explicit $f in bb(Z)_p[[T]]$ for which $v_p ((D^a f)(0)) = 0$ for all $a >= 0$. Contrast this with Theorem 8.21 for a height-$2$ formal group.
